      "clipboard_restored": "Oh man, there’s some good conspira-lore around the entire Nvidia/Jensen situation. All of the affairs had been going on for years, basically. The reason it broke now was a strategic move by Anyhropic’s co-founder to get Jensen out of the way to accomplish two things:\n\n1. True export controls against China.\n2. Banning open source models.\n\nJensen fought very publicly against both, and if you look at them together, I think what you see is both a pickaxe sales man wanting to drive up the utility and cost of his pickaxes… but also, the same argument I have been making — the most dangerous future is one where closed models win, and open models are banned. It guarantees these companies control of the future. Want to know how I know Jensen was aware of this? In an interview after he want vocally on record about not banning open models, he talks about how he went on the record against it, and make a joke about having saved humanity in the process. The joke is never explained."
    },
